-- title:
--   Degree-zero cohomological flatness of the integral model at level p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak X$ be a term of `DRModelPackage p`, that is, a bundle of data and properties for the scheme `DRModel p` over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$: here `DRModel p` is the two-chart integral model $\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\ \mathbf Z\ F\ j$ attached to the field $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p` and the element $j=$ `IgusaScheme.jFull p`, namely the pushout glueing the spectra of the two $\mathbf Z$-subalgebras of $F$ generated by $j$ and by $j^{-1}$, and `DRModel.toBase p` is the induced morphism to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$; the package records in particular that this morphism is proper and flat, that the scheme is integral and normal on affine opens, together with curve models of $F$ over $\mathbf Q$ and over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ identified with the corresponding base changes and their Galois and place compatibilities, two sections over $\mathbf Z$, and a smooth locus with its maximality property. The assertion is that for every commutative ring $A$ equipped with a $\mathbf Z$-algebra structure, the structure map
--   $$A \longrightarrow \Gamma\bigl(\,\mathfrak X_A,\ \mathcal O\,\bigr),\qquad \mathfrak X_A=\mathrm{DRModel}\ p\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z}\operatorname{Spec}A,$$
--   is bijective, the $A$-algebra structure on the global sections being the one induced by the second projection of the pullback via `Scheme.TwoAffineOpenCover.algebraOfHom`.
--
--   This is cohomological flatness in degree $0$ for the Deligne–Rapoport integral model: $c_*\mathcal O = \mathcal O$ holds universally for the structure morphism $c$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$. It supplies the degree-zero global sections input to the relative Picard package for this model, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.nonempty_legTwoInputV2`](thm.html#ModularCurve.nonempty_legTwoInputV2).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackage_bijective_algebraMap_sections_baseChange.lean

